details.image_prompt:
[
  "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The scene features two shallow matte ceramic bowls placed on a rustic, aged oak wooden table with visible grain and slight knife marks. The camera angle is a 3/4 overhead view, capturing the full contents of both bowls. One bowl is in sharp focus in the foreground, while the second is softly blurred in the background. Each bowl contains a generous portion of fluffy, golden-brown whole-wheat couscous as a base, topped with a tender, opaque white halibut fillet that displays a light golden sear from the pan. Beside the fish, a mixture of blistered, bright red cherry tomatoes, dark Kalamata olives, and wilted, deep green baby spinach is spooned, creating a rustic, colorful saucy texture. Small amounts of the tomato-infused vegetable broth pool slightly at the base of the couscous. Props include a tarnished silver fork resting casually on the wood surface near the primary bowl and a few stray, halved cherry tomatoes and a single pitted Kalamata olive scattered naturally on the table nearby. The lighting is soft and natural, streaming from a window on the left, casting gentle shadows and creating a slight, authentic sheen on the olive oil and tomato juices. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene should look like someone just finished cooking and plating — lived-in, warm, authentic. Not a sterile studio setup. Slight natural imperfections: an asymmetric garnish placement, a small sauce drip on the bowl rim, slightly uneven browning on the fish. Include subtle traces of the cooking process: a few grains of couscous and a tiny fragment of spinach leaf on the table. No plastic sheen, no unnaturally smooth surfaces, no perfect symmetry. Warm, golden-hour color temperature — cozy and inviting, not cold or clinical. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. The image should be indistinguishable from a photograph taken by a professional food photographer for a printed cookbook."
]
